## Upgrades

### An application or chart version

```bash
task maintenance:check-versions           # what is outdated, across every source
task maintenance:update-version SERVICE=<name>
task flux:sync-versions
git add ansible/inventories/prod/group_vars/all.yml \
        kubernetes/infrastructure/sources/versions-configmap.yaml
git commit -m "Bump <name>"
```

`task maintenance:update-all-versions` does the same for every outdated pin at
once. Versions are pinned deliberately: nothing tracks `latest`, and no bot
merges bumps unattended — the scheduled job opens one merge request and leaves
it for a human.

### Host packages

```bash
task maintenance:update-packages          # add -- -e auto_reboot=true to reboot
task maintenance:update-applications      # host-level apps to their pinned versions
task maintenance:update-full              # both, rolling and interactive
task infra:verify
```

Silence the alerts a planned restart will trip **before** starting, or the next
real incident arrives in a channel everyone has learned to ignore. There is no
task for this; go through Alertmanager directly:

```bash
kubectl get svc -n observability                     # find the Alertmanager service
kubectl -n observability port-forward svc/<alertmanager-svc> 9093:9093
# then http://localhost:9093 → Silences → New Silence
```

### Kubernetes nodes

```bash
# bump k3s_version in group_vars/all.yml, then:
task maintenance:update-k3s-nodes         # drains, upgrades and uncordons node by node
task k3s:status
```

Servers first, one at a time, watching the etcd quorum. Rolling back is a
version bump in the other direction plus the same task.
`task maintenance:update-cluster` chains the node upgrade and the pin sweep.

### The platform library

Bumping `lib_ref` upgrades the Ansible collection, the CI templates and the
Terraform modules together. Read the library's changelog first
([weisssrv-lib](https://git.ericsweiss.com/eric/weisssrv-lib), and
`ansible_collections/weisssrv/infra/MIGRATING.md` for role-level breaking
changes), then:

```bash
task ansible:install-collections    # re-installs at the new ref
task lib:sync                       # refresh .weisssrv-lib, the vendored scripts' source
task lint
```

### The template itself

See § Updating the template.

